{
  "title": "Che lo {csi:sapesse} o no, poco {ip:importa}",
  "translation": "Whether he knew or not hardly matters",
  "topics": "Choosing mood and tense according to meaning, including the less common forms",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      {
        "h": "From rules to meaning"
      },
      "There are no new forms here. The point is that a competent writer can change a mood and thereby change what's being said.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Sentence",
            "What it implies"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{ip:Cerco} una casa che {ip:ha} il giardino.",
              "I have a particular house in mind."
            ],
            [
              "{ip:Cerco} una casa che {csp:abbia} il giardino.",
              "Any house with a garden will do."
            ],
            [
              "Non {ip:dico} che {ip:ha} torto.",
              "He is wrong, but I'm not saying so."
            ],
            [
              "Non {ip:dico} che {csp:abbia} torto.",
              "I'm not claiming that he is wrong."
            ],
            [
              "{ip:Temo} che {fs:verrà}.",
              "I'm afraid that he will come: I expect it."
            ],
            [
              "{ip:Temo} che {csp:venga}.",
              "I'm afraid that he may come."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "A denied cause"
      },
      "A cause that's being rejected isn't asserted, so it takes the *congiuntivo*: *{pp:È partito} perché {im:era} stanco*, but *{pp:È partito} non perché {csi:fosse} stanco, ma perché si annoiava*.",
      {
        "h": "Forms worth having in your range"
      },
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Form",
            "Example",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Alternative with che",
              "Che lo {csi:sapesse} o no, poco {ip:importa}.",
              "whether… or not"
            ],
            [
              "Exhortation",
              "{imv:Dicano} pure ciò che {ip:vogliono}.",
              "let them…"
            ],
            [
              "Come se",
              "{ip:Parla} come se {csi:sapesse} tutto.",
              "as if"
            ],
            [
              "Comparison",
              "{ip:È} più difficile di quanto {csi:pensassi}.",
              "than I thought"
            ],
            [
              "Future of doubt",
              "{fs:Sarà}, ma non ci {ip:credo}.",
              "that may be, but…"
            ],
            [
              "Exclamatory infinitive",
              "Io, tradirti?",
              "indignant rejection"
            ],
            [
              "Conditional in a question",
              "{cop:Sarebbe} a dire?",
              "meaning what?"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "When more than one form is right"
      },
      "After *{ip:spero} che*, both *{imv:venga}* and *{fs:verrà}* are correct: the future sounds more confident. After *{ip:credo} che*, the indicative is heard in speech, but it lowers the register. The skill at this level isn't knowing what's possible, but knowing what each choice says about you."
    ]
  },
